---
import BlogPostLayout from '../../../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro';

const title = "Bad and Worst Career Advice to Ignore in India and How to Judge Any Advice";
const seoTitle = "Bad Career Advice to Ignore and How to Judge Any Advice in India";
const description = "Bad and worst career advice in India: common myths, how to test advice, who to ask and a twelve-week method with honest limits.";
const seoDescription = "Test every piece of advice against evidence and your own situation.";
const canonical = "https://futurecareerschool.com/blog/career-guidance/bad-and-worst-career-advice-to-ignore-and-how-to-judge-any-advice-india/";
const publishedDateISO = "2026-10-30";
const publishedDateLabel = "30 October 2026";
const authorName = "Shivanshi Sehgal";
const authorUrl = "https://futurecareerschool.com/about/shivanshi-sehgal/";
const authorRole = "Career researcher and writer";

const faqItems = [
  [
    "What is the worst career advice?",
    "Advice that ignores your finances, strengths and evidence, and claims to work for everyone."
  ],
  [
    "Who should I ask?",
    "People two to five years ahead on the path you consider, plus one sceptic."
  ],
  [
    "Should I ignore my family advice?",
    "Listen, test it and share your evidence respectfully."
  ],
  [
    "How do I judge online advice?",
    "Check who gives it, what they gain and whether they show evidence."
  ],
  [
    "How many people should I ask?",
    "At least five, including people who left the field."
  ],
  [
    "How do I avoid fraud?",
    "Never pay for guaranteed placement."
  ],
  [
    "Will AI change this?",
    "It helps learning and planning. Judgement remains yours."
  ]
];

const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    name: item.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { "@type": "Answer", text: item.a },
  })),
};
---

<BlogPostLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  seoTitle={seoTitle}
  seoDescription={seoDescription}
  canonical={canonical}
  category="career-guidance"
  publishedAt={publishedDateISO}
  publishedLabel={publishedDateLabel}
  authorName={authorName}
  authorUrl={authorUrl}
  authorRole={authorRole}
  jsonLdExtras={[faqJsonLd]}
>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>Bad career advice often sounds confident and universal, such as follow your passion blindly, only one degree matters or take what your friends take, so test any advice by asking who gives it, what evidence supports it, what it costs to try and whether it fits your finances and strengths, then run a small test before committing.</strong> The decisions that unlock high income opportunities include choosing a branch early and building a high-income skill portfolio of finished work, because AI can handle routine tasks but cannot take responsibility for your results.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Short answer:</strong> Test every piece of advice against evidence and your own situation.</li>
      <li><strong>Evidence:</strong> This page quotes no statistics or pay figures and was not built from fetched sources. Ten live notices and two conversations, as set out below, are the best way to get current local evidence.</li>
      <li><strong>Growth:</strong> Clear proof and finished work support an earlier path to financial freedom.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <p>
