          <td data-label="Check first">Check real notices and alumni paths</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Route"><strong>Take what everyone is taking</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Good fit when">Crowded routes carry competition and mismatch</td>
          <td data-label="Check first">Ask what fraction of people succeed</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Route"><strong>Government job or nothing</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Good fit when">Public jobs suit some people, but private and own routes exist</td>
          <td data-label="Check first">List both with real requirements</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Route"><strong>Pay first, always</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Good fit when">Learning and fit affect long term earning</td>
          <td data-label="Check first">Compare income and growth over three years</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="bcmythb">A check before you act</h2>

  <p>
    Follow the ten percent rule of household income for education and aim for a caution limit of twenty percent. Example figures are an illustration, not a real fee.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
