          <td data-label="Question">Do I enjoy the daily work?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Test it for a week</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Cost</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">What will this cost in time and money?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Compare free and paid options</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Entry</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">What do real notices or people ask for?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Read five notices</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Check"><strong>Growth</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Question">What does year three look like?</td>
          <td data-label="Tip">Ask two people</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="bcmythc">A twelve-week plan</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Weeks</th>
          <th>Task</th>
          <th>Output</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Weeks"><strong>1 to 2</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Task">Read five notices or listings and list what they ask for</td>
          <td data-label="Output">Requirements table</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Weeks"><strong>3 to 5</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Task">Talk to three people who took this path and note what helped</td>
          <td data-label="Output">Interview notes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Weeks"><strong>6 to 9</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Task">Pick one piece of advice you were given, define a small test for it and run it for four weeks</td>
          <td data-label="Output">Bridge project</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Weeks"><strong>10 to 12</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Task">Act on the decision and write a short review note</td>
          <td data-label="Output">Decision note</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="bajudge">Five questions to ask about any piece of advice</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Question</th>
          <th>Why</th>
          <th>Example</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Question"><strong>Who is giving it?</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why">Experience and bias differ</td>
          <td data-label="Example">A person who succeeded in a different era may not know today</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Question"><strong>What do they gain?</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why">Sellers and coaches may benefit</td>
          <td data-label="Example">A course seller praising courses</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Question"><strong>What evidence supports it?</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why">Stories are not data</td>
          <td data-label="Example">Notices, outcomes, alumni records</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Question"><strong>What does it cost to test?</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why">Small tests are safer</td>
          <td data-label="Example">A free course before a paid one</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Question"><strong>Does it fit my situation?</strong></td>
          <td data-label="Why">Money, location and family differ</td>
          <td data-label="Example">Advice for a metro may not fit a small town</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>
    Write the answers down before you act. Advice that survives these questions is usually worth testing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Advice that fails them is still useful as a reminder of what to check.
  </p>

  <h2 id="basurvive">Survivorship bias in success stories</h2>

  <p>
    Many popular career stories come from people who took a risk and succeeded. We rarely hear from the many who took the same risk and struggled.
  </p>
  <p>
    Ask for the average path, not only the famous one.
  </p>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Story type</th>
          <th>What is missing</th>
          <th>Question to ask</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Story type"><strong>Dropped out and became rich</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What is missing">Most dropouts do not</td>
          <td data-label="Question to ask">How many tried and how many succeeded?</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Story type"><strong>Cracked a hard exam in a few months</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What is missing">Many spent years</td>
          <td data-label="Question to ask">What is the typical preparation time?</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td data-label="Story type"><strong>Quit a job and started a business</strong></td>
          <td data-label="What is missing">Many closed within years</td>
          <td data-label="Question to ask">What savings and support did they have?</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

